// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-10-15 (Thursday): Pure math sequence — the Catalan numbers
// ============================================================================
//
// THE SEQUENCE (OEIS A000108): C(n) = (2n choose n)/(n+1). C0..C5 =
// 1, 1, 2, 5, 14, 42. C(n) counts the number of distinct ways to validly
// nest n pairs of parentheses (equivalently: full binary trees with n
// internal nodes). C(3) = 5 is the number this piece is actually built
// from — the 5 valid nestings of 3 bracket pairs:
//   A ((()))   B (()())   C (())()   D ()(())   E ()()()
//
// THE MUSICAL MAPPING: for each structure, track nesting DEPTH after every
// token (open = +1, close = -1), then map depth -> scale degree (depth 0 =
// tonic, 1 = third, 2 = fifth, 3 = octave) — a real leap, not a step, per
// level of nesting:
//   A depths 1,2,3,2,1,0 -> degrees 2 4 7 4 2 0   (one arch, all the way up)
//   B depths 1,2,1,2,1,0 -> degrees 2 4 2 4 2 0   (two shallower arches)
//   C depths 1,2,1,0,1,0 -> degrees 2 4 2 0 2 0   (one arch, then flat)
//   D depths 1,0,1,2,1,0 -> degrees 2 0 2 4 2 0   (flat, then one arch)
//   E depths 1,0,1,0,1,0 -> degrees 2 0 2 0 2 0   (pure pendulum, no nesting)
// Played in that order (A->E), the piece's own phrase development performs
// an actual mathematical fact: as C(3)'s five structures run out, the
// melodic contour literally collapses from deepest nesting (A, reaching the
// octave) to no nesting at all (E, alternating flat) — structure, not
// decoration.
//
// CYCLES 6-10 restate A-E RETROGRADE (each note order reversed — jazz-improv
// device #1) and lifted an octave (+7 degrees) as the climax register (the
// Goa-trance pitch-lift convention, MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §6, used here because
// it's free: no new layer, same five structures, now read backwards and up
// an octave). Degree 0 recurs as the anchor every phrase closes on — the
// structural tone every nesting always resolves back to (device #2).
//
// FILTER AUTOMATION tracks each structure's own MAX DEPTH, not an arbitrary
// LFO: A(3) brightest, B/C/D(2) mid, E(1) darkest, then all five scaled up
// 1.5x for the lifted retrograde pass — the cutoff literally reports how
// deeply each structure nests.
//
// SCALE: D:major — fresh tonic/mode for this slot (prior Thursdays: C minor
// pentatonic, D harmonic minor, E phrygian, D dorian, A aeolian, E
// mixolydian, G lydian); plain major suits pure counting, no borrowed color.
//
// ARRANGEMENT: lead is `square` (sharp/discrete, MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §1) — a
// combinatorics topic reads better austere than lush, and it's unused on a
// recent Thursday (Padovan: supersaw, Thue-Morse: sawtooth). Drone is a
// doubled-octave UNISON on the tonic (sine, pure/soft) rather than a dyad of
// two different notes — standing for C(0)=C(1)=1, the recurrence's two equal
// base cases, not an arbitrary interval. NO percussion: nesting depth has no
// inherent metric pulse, and the two numbers this topic needs an audible
// outlet for (which structure is playing, how deep it nests) are already
// spent on the phrase alternation itself and the depth-tracking filter — a
// drum layer would be a third, decorative outlet for numbers already heard.
//
// TEMPO: setcpm(26), 4 quarter-note beats/cycle = 104 BPM. No genre-specific
// tempo mandate on a math-sequence day. CYCLES: 10. 26 x 10 / 60 = 23.08s.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(26)

$lead: n(`<
  [2 ~ 4 7 ~ 4 2 0]
  [2 ~ 4 2 ~ 4 2 0]
  [2 ~ 4 2 ~ 0 2 0]
  [2 ~ 0 2 ~ 4 2 0]
  [2 ~ 0 2 ~ 0 2 0]
  [7 ~ 9 11 ~ 14 11 9]
  [7 ~ 9 11 ~ 9 11 9]
  [7 ~ 9 7 ~ 9 11 9]
  [7 ~ 9 11 ~ 9 7 9]
  [7 ~ 9 7 ~ 9 7 9]
>`)
  .scale("D:major")
  .sound("square")
  .attack(.01).decay(.12).sustain(.1).release(.18)
  .lpf(`<1600 1100 1100 1100 600 2400 1650 1650 1650 900>`)
  .lpq(3)
  .gain(.4)
  .room(1.1)

$drone: n("0 7").scale("D:major")
  .sound("sine")
  .attack(1.2).release(2)
  .lpf(500)
  .gain(.2)
  .room(2.4)
